# Normalise line endings in the repository.
#
# WHY. Two commits on this fork rewrote eight files from LF to CRLF wholesale -- 5,734
# lines of pure line-ending churn across engine/, moe/ and server/. Against upstream the
# diff read 7,303 insertions and 4,910 deletions; ignoring whitespace, 2,443 and 50. The
# rest was noise that made the fork's actual changes unreadable and would have conflicted
# on every line of those files at the next rebase.
#
# text=auto tells git to store text files with LF and check them out with the platform's
# convention; eol=lf pins the working copy too, so an editor on Windows cannot quietly
# reintroduce the same problem.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, byte for byte.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gguf binary
*.safetensors binary
*.so binary
*.whl binary
